    "narrative": "Our offensive focus for July 7 centers on capitalizing on high-ceiling matchups against pitchers with vulnerable xERAs. **Bryce Harper** (74.19) is our clear anchor today; he faces Abbott, A, whose 5.07 xERA provides a massive boost to **Bryce Harper**\u2019s elite xwOBA profile. **Taylor Ward** (66.83) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (65.48) round out our top-tier targets. **Taylor Ward** benefits immensely from a favorable park factor (+16%) and a strong lead-off position, while **Geraldo Perdomo**\u2019s high score is driven by a standout matchup against M\u00e1rquez (5.64 xERA), allowing him to leverage his plate discipline for optimal run production. We are also tracking the stolen base potential for **Daulton Varsho** and **Tyler Freeman**; both earn efficiency bumps due to their opposing pitchers\u2019 slow deliveries, making them essential pivots in our pursuit of the scarce SB category.\n\nThe decision to bench **Jung Hoo Lee** (42.41) was razor-thin. While **Jung Hoo Lee** remains a viable depth piece, he narrowly missed the starting cut because his profile against Miles (3.12 xERA) failed to surpass the upside of **Gavin Sheets** (60.46) or **Tyler Freeman** (60.52). The optimizer favored **Gavin Sheets** for his stronger platoon advantage and power ceiling against Gallen. We are also wary of the risks posed to **Zack Gelof** (48.97) and **Dylan Beavers** (43.29), both of whom must contend with Skubal and Boyd, respectively; while **Zack Gelof** maintains value through a lead-off spot, he faces an elite arm that suppresses his overall efficiency score. We continue to monitor the status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** on the IL and ensure that non-starters like **Lawrence Butler** remain benched to preserve our game caps for more favorable defensive sets.",
